{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-05-scope-test-cost.md at exact 6acfa2620418bc943165f8b2e1d4f84d1d0e6156 on request/scope-test-cost, under promise git:sha1…ddfb514 on request git:sha1…082884e\n\nScope test cost at 6acfa2620418bc943165f8b2e1d4f84d1d0e6156 on request/scope-test-cost (main 06381163 plus this change). Primary subject: notes/2026-10-05-scope-test-cost.md, the measurements and what they show. Finding: the scope runtime is not the cause of the cost. 400 acts on one scope cost the same per 50 from first to last (observed), and the pinned definition is validated once. Two growths are in the test pool: a call through SELF.fetch or the API service binding gets slower with the number of such calls in a run (27 ms per 50 at first, 650 ms after 250; an empty route that reaches no object grows the same way, and the time is spent before the handler is entered); and creating a Durable Object gets slower with the number made in the run (a bare object with no product code grows the same way). The exact cause inside the pool was not found. Change, tests only: the replay, founding, texts and one lane test read histories by calling the Worker's route function directly in the test's isolate, which is the function the Worker's fetch runs, in place of SELF.fetch; about 135 of the 176 entrypoint calls of a run were these. routes.test.ts and client.test.ts keep one test per route and per binding. No test was removed and no assertion changed. Measured, observed, three runs each, shared machine, warm: scope project wall time 4.75 to 4.83 s before, 3.89 to 3.95 s after; whole vitest run 5.38 to 5.52 s before, 5.11 to 5.14 s after. The saving is larger than the fitted growth predicted, and the note says the reason was not found. Recommended and not done, with estimates, in the note: going below about 3 s for the scope project needs fewer acts and deliveries, which means merging or removing tests after an audit of their invariants. Gate at this head, one run: 285 vitest and 3 node tests pass.","body":{"commit":"6acfa2620418bc943165f8b2e1d4f84d1d0e6156","path":"notes/2026-10-05-scope-test-cost.md"}}